{{Quote|This is a T-6 shuttle. One of the more ''useful'' ships in the Jedi fleet.|[[Berem Khana]], to [[Soona Taj]]|<ref name="Jedi Knights 8">[[Jedi Knights 8|''Jedi Knights'' 8]]</ref>}}
The '''T-6 shuttle''', also called the '''Jedi T-6 shuttle''', or the '''T-6 Jedi Shuttle''', was an unarmed [[transport]] used by the [[Jedi Order]]. An older design, it saw greater use during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Databank T6" /> By the [[time]] of the [[early rebellion against the Galactic Empire]], the [[shuttle]] [[cockpit]] was used in the design of the [[A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter]].<ref name="RSOM">''[[Rebel Starfighters Owners' Workshop Manual]]''</ref>

==Characteristics==
[[File:JediT6Shuttle-SWChrome2024.png|thumb|280px|left|A T-6 shuttle in horizontal flight configuration.]]
Manufactured by the [[Verpine]] hives of [[Slayn & Korpil]],<ref name="StarfightersEncyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref> the semicircular T-6 [[shuttle]] featured a rotating engine block and [[cockpit]] that oriented with the rest of the ship when landed or in flight. In its landing configuration, the ship sat horizontally, supported by a trio of landing gear. The cockpit, somewhat conical in shape, remained aligned with the body of the craft, with the three engines likewise horizontally aligned with the body of the shuttle. When entering flight mode, the cockpit and the engine block rotated ninety degrees. The craft had one loading ramp, located on the port side of the engine block. Shuttles of this class featured [[ejector seat]]s that, when launched, enclosed the being in a flexible, cushioned [[survival capsule]].<ref name="CotF" />

Due to its role as an ambassadorial craft, the T-6 shuttle lacked weaponry, but was equipped with a [[hyperdrive]]. Furthermore, the craft's spacious interior provided for reasonably comfortable [[Realspace|space]] travel. When pressed into service during the [[Clone Wars]], [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] T-6 shuttles were adorned with a [[Republic crest|Galactic Roundel]] and painted in the red-and-white color scheme of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]], though they remained unarmed.<ref name="StarfightersEncyclopedia" /> Decades later, T-6 shuttles that were a part of the [[Citizens' Fleet|fleet]] assembled by [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] were equipped with aftermarket weaponry added on either side of the cockpit.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==History==
{{Quote|There's nothing you could have done to avoid a crash, master. I've never seen such a dense debris field around a planet. I don't think even Plo Koon could have gotten a T-6 through it safely.|[[Anakin Skywalker]] comforts [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] over crashing a T-6 shuttle on the [[planet]] [[Carnelion IV]]|<ref name="Obi-Wan and Anakin 1">[[Obi-Wan and Anakin 1|''Obi-Wan and Anakin'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:GrievousConfrontsJediPadawan-AORGrievous1.png|thumb|left|300px|[[General]] [[Grievous]] stands atop a T-6 shuttle during the Clone Wars.]]
T-6 shuttles were designed for the [[Jedi Order]], which employed the craft since between [[68 BBY]] and around [[58 BBY]]<ref name="Date 42BBY">{{TalesDate|J2}}</ref> when [[Jedi Master]]s [[Dooku]] and [[Mace Windu]] took one on a [[Mission to Raxus Secundus (Mace Windu and Dooku)|journey]] to [[Raxus Secundus]].<ref name="Choices">{{TOTJ|Choices}}</ref> In [[32 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Jedi Master [[Sifo-Dyas|Sifo Dyas]] was shot down in a T-6 shuttle over the [[Oba Diah moon]].<ref name="The Lost One">{{TCW|The Lost One}}</ref>

During the [[Clone Wars]], following the [[Attempted kidnapping of Roo-Roo Page|capture]] of the [[Duros]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Cad Bane]], the T-6 shuttle was used to [[Mission to Black Stall Station|transport]] Jedi Masters Mace Windu and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], Bane, and [[Clone Commander]] [[Cody|CC-2224]] to Bane's [[Black Stall Station|hideout]] in the [[asteroid]]-strewn [[Rogue Antar system]] to retrieve a stolen [[holocron]]. However, the [[space station]] proved to be a trap—Bane eluded his captors and activated the hideout's [[Self-destruct mechanism|self-destruct sequence]] before departing in an [[escape pod]]. Windu, Kenobi, and [[Commander]] Cody left in their shuttle with the recovered holocron before the station exploded.<ref name="CoF">{{TCW|Children of the Force}}</ref>

[[File:T6Shuttle-BH.png|thumb|right|300px|A T-6 shuttle being attacked by a vulture droid]]
Following the destruction of the [[Felucia Medical Station HCTFF2|Felucia medical station]], Jedi [[Anakin Skywalker]], Obi-Wan Kenobi, and [[Ahsoka Tano]] took a T-6 shuttle to [[Felucia]] to [[Skirmish on Felucia|investigate]] the [[Haven-class medical station|medical center's]] disappearance. Upon their arrival, the shuttle was attacked by [[Vulture-class starfighter|vulture droids]] launched from a [[Automated vulture droid deployment station|deployment pod]]. The [[droid starfighter]]s shot and disabled the unarmed shuttle, but the trio of Jedi escaped using their ejector seats before the shuttle collided with a [[mountain]] on the planet's surface.<ref name="Bounty Hunters">{{TCW|Bounty Hunters (episode)}}</ref>

Around [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Date 21BBY">{{TCWcanondates|222}}</ref> Jedi [[Plo Koon]] and Ahsoka Tano used a T-6 shuttle to travel to [[Florrum]] in search of the [[bounty]] hunters [[Boba Fett]], [[Aurra Sing]], and [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]], who had taken hostages from the crew of the [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|Star Destroyer]] ''[[Endurance]]''. The Jedi confronted the renegades on the planet and rescued two of the hostages, capturing Fett and Bossk in the process. The T-6 shuttle was then used to transport the Republic forces and their captives to the [[Republic Judiciary Central Detention Center]] on Coruscant.<ref name="LT">{{TCW|Lethal Trackdown}}</ref>

Another T-6 shuttle was used by Padawan Tano and [[Pantoran]] [[Senator]] [[Riyo Chuchi]] to travel to a [[Trade Federation]] [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|Droid Control Ship]] above [[Pantora]] during their search for the kidnapped daughters of Pantoran [[Chairman]] [[Notluwiski Papanoida]].<ref name="SOI">{{TCW|Sphere of Influence}}</ref>

Obi-Wan Kenobi and Anakin Skywalker later used a shuttle to journey to [[Dathomir]] to uncover the origins of a [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] warrior, [[Savage Opress]], who was responsible for the [[Skirmish in the Temple of Eedit|deaths]] of [[Halsey|two]] [[Knox|Jedi]]. After learning that Opress was on [[Toydaria]], the duo took the craft to the [[Toydarian]] [[homeworld]] to [[Showdown at Toydaria|confront]] the [[Dark Acolyte|acolyte]]. The shuttle was destroyed by Opress as he made his escape.<ref name="WOTM">{{TCW|Witches of the Mist}}</ref>

[[File:StuckOnPeridea-Ahsoka.png|thumb|left|300px|Ahsoka Tano's T-6 shuttle]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], T-6 shuttles was a sign assistance was on the way. After [[Order 66|destruction of the Jedi Order]], the T-6 became a rarer sight. Years later, the T-6's recognizable silhouette still symbolized hope.<ref name="SWECG">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> 

Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Ahsoka Series Date">{{AhsokaSeriesDate}}</ref> after the [[Attack on the Vesper|Attack on the ''Vesper'']],<ref name="Ahoska episode 1">{{Ahsoka|Part One: Master and Apprentice}}</ref> [[Ahsoka Tano]] used [[T-6 1974|one]] of these [[starship]]s to travel to [[Lothal]] and pick up [[Sabine Wren]], in order to begin their [[Quest to find Ezra Bridger|search]] for the [[Jedi]] [[Ezra Bridger]].<ref name="Family Reunion – and Farewell">{{Rebels|Family Reunion &ndash; and Farewell}}</ref> 

A number of T-6 shuttles were retrofitted with armament and participated in the [[Battle of Exegol]] as part of the [[Citizens' Fleet]] of over 14,000 starships to aid the [[Resistance]] in their fight against the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:T-6_on_Alderaan.png|thumb|250px|A T-6 shuttle docked at an [[Alderaan]]ian city]]
The T-6 shuttle first appeared in ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="CotF">{{TCW|Children of the Force}}</ref>

The [http://www.starwars.com/explore/the-clone-wars/ep501/#!/media/slideshow online guide] for "[[Revival (episode)|Revival]]," the first episode of [[The Clone Wars: Season Five|''The Clone Wars'': Season Five]], incorrectly identifies an [[Eta-class shuttle|''Eta''-class shuttle]] as a T-6 shuttle.<ref name="Revival guide">{{SW|url=explore/the-clone-wars/ep501|text="Revival" - ''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide|nolive=1}}</ref>

